--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--   Test Description                                                               --
--   This test is composed in different phases:                                     --
----------------------------- First Phase --------------------------------------------
--   This is a simple test which shows that when a screener is programmed           --
--   To drop a frame when matches it, then the frame is actually dropped.           --
--   16 frames are received, one for each type1 screener and every screener is      --
--   programmed to drop the frame in case of match, therefore all the frames will   --
--   be dropped.                                                                    --
---------------------------- Second Phase --------------------------------------------
--   Here we want to make sure that, when a frame is matched by more than one       --
--   screener, then if the screeners have a different setting on drop_on_match      --
--   the frame must be dropped anyway since it is matched by at least one scrn      --
--   with drop_on_match bit set. Reg0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14 will be tested as they       --
--   will have drop_on_match set wheread Reg1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15 will have it unset   --
---------------------------- Third Phase ---------------------------------------------
--   Here we want to make sure that, when a frame is matched by more than one       --
--   screener, then if the screeners have a different setting on drop_on_match      --
--   the frame must be dropped anyway since it is matched by at least one scrn      --
--   with drop_on_match bit set. Reg1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15 will be tested as they       --
--   will have drop_on_match set wheread Reg0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14 will have it unset   --
